quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  24,21,"O believers! Do not follow in the footsteps of Satan. And whoever follows in Satan’s steps (should know that) he indeed prompts you to indecency and evil. And were it not for Allah’s grace and His mercy upon you, none of you would ever have been pure (from the stain of such slander). But Allah purifies whomever He pleases, and Allah is All-Hearing, All-Knowing."
  24,22,"Let the people of grace and bounty from you not swear against giving (charity) to the relatives, the needy and the emigrants in Allah’s way. They should pardon and overlook (their mistake). Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  24,23,"Indeed, those who accuse chaste believing women who are unaware (of indecency) shall be cursed in this world and the Hereafter. And there shall be a great punishment for them,"
  24,24,"on the Day when their tongues, their hands, and their feet testify against them concerning whatever they used to do."
  24,25,"On that Day, Allah will pay them their just due in full. And they shall know that Allah is the Manifest Truth."
  24,26,"Wicked women are for wicked men, and wicked men are for wicked women. Virtuous women are for virtuous men, and virtuous men are for virtuous women.* These (chaste people) are innocent of what they (the slanderers) say (about them). They shall have forgiveness and honourable provision."
  24,27,O believers! Do not enter houses other than yours until you ask permission and greet their residents. That is better for you. Perhaps you may become mindful of advice.
